00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.160
That's our band, the How I Met Your Mother theme song, The Salads.
那是我们的乐队，《老爸老妈浪漫史》的主题曲，The Salads乐队。

300
00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:12.880
Yeah, that's us.
没错，那就是我们。

301
00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:13.580
Is that right?
是这样吗？

302
00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:16.120
Carter and I met in college playing in bands together.
我和卡特是在大学玩乐队时认识的。

303
00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.660
We were writing songs together before we were writing TV together.
我们在一起写歌的时间比一起写剧本的时间还要早。

304
00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.880
And we did, our band, The Salads, did the theme song.
我们的乐队“沙拉乐队”确实创作了那首主题曲。

305
00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:27.180
I'm very honored, Josh, to be mentioned in the same breath as the Office theme song, which I think is a total banger.
乔什，能和《办公室》的主题曲相提并论，我感到非常荣幸，我觉得那首歌简直太棒了。

306
00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:30.560
And I had not heard it in a minute because I hadn't rewatched it in a while.
而且我有一阵子没听了，因为我已经很久没重温这部剧了。

307
00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:34.180
I wrote down, one of my notes was, God, this theme song kicks ass.
我当时写下的一条笔记就是：天哪，这主题曲太带感了。

308
00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:36.440
Like, it just gets you so excited, the theme song.
就是那种，这主题曲真的能让你瞬间兴奋起来。

309
00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.160
It's true.
确实如此。

310
00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.500
Both of them, every time I hear them, I get happy.
这两部剧的主题曲，每次听到我都会很开心。

311
00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.140
I'm like, okay.
我就觉得，好吧，开始了。

312
00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:41.660
It makes you happy.
它确实让人心情愉悦。

313
00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:42.060
Yeah.
没错。

314
00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:42.520
Yeah.
是啊。

315
00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.340
So true.
太对了。

316
00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:44.120
It does.
确实如此。

317
00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:52.840
I think one of the things I like about both of the shows is that that redemption moment where there is a character that is struggling with something.
我觉得这两部剧我最喜欢的一点，就是那种救赎时刻，当某个角色正陷入困境时。

318
00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.080
And there's always that moment where your heart takes a turn.
总会有那么一个瞬间，让你心头一颤。

319
00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.520
And I thought you guys did that so well.
我觉得你们处理得非常好。

320
00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:00.480
And I love the moment.
我特别喜欢那个瞬间。

321
00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:04.180
One of my favorite moments in this episode is between Michael and Kelly.
这一集中我最喜欢的时刻之一，就是迈克尔和凯莉之间的互动。

322
00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:05.520
Yeah.
没错。

323
00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:13.980
And when he shares how much he struggles and he gets really honest with her in a way that's not performative for the camera the way he normally is, Josh.
当他向她倾诉自己的挣扎，并以一种非表演性的、不像平时那样对着镜头做作的方式与她坦诚相待时，乔什。

324
00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.920
He is kind of like the pick me, like character, but he was just really honest with her.
他平时就像那种渴望关注的角色，但那一刻他真的对她敞开了心扉。

325
00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:22.960
And I used to love that transition moment for Michael.
我以前就很喜欢迈克尔那种转变的时刻。

326
00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:23.560
Yeah.
是啊。

327
00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:34.400
You know, it also occurs to me, like, a question one might ask themselves is, like, why is this film crew still filming these people?
你知道，我突然想到，人们可能会问的一个问题是：为什么摄制组还要一直拍这些人？

328
00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:35.260
Yes.
没错。

329
00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:44.040
But the way I think about it is, like, a person with a really good filmmaking eye would be like, these are fascinating people.
但我认为，一个拥有敏锐电影视角的人会觉得，这些人太迷人了。

330
00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.760
Like, there's a fascinating story going on here.
这里正在上演一个引人入胜的故事。

331
00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.460
And it's not about kings and queens and it's not about super wealthy people.
它讲的不是国王和王后，也不是超级富豪。

332
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.560
It's about people.
它讲的是普通人。

333
00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:58.860
And just, there were moments, you know, with Jim and Pam over the years that were like Chekhov.
多年来，吉姆和帕姆之间的一些时刻，简直就像契诃夫笔下的情节。

334
00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:06.700
Like, they're like, they're like, you know, like a, you know, in the Jane Austen or something, like the fingertips graze together.
就像简·奥斯汀小说里的那种感觉，比如指尖轻轻触碰。

335
00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.780
And it's just like magic, like big firework kind of thing.
那就像魔法一样，有着巨大的火花。

336
00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:16.240
And I feel like the modesty of it is actually what gives it its mythic quality, if that makes sense.
我觉得正是这种平实感赋予了它某种神话般的特质，不知道这么说你能不能理解。

337
00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.160
Like, that it's just really about people in Scranton.
因为它讲的真的只是斯克兰顿普通人的故事。

338
00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:26.860
And if you ever watch, that's why I think I, in some ways, I love documentaries even more than regular filMs.
如果你仔细观察，这就是为什么在某些方面，我甚至比普通电影更喜欢纪录片。

339
00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:31.820
Because watching people behave in an unselfconscious way.
因为看着人们展现出不加修饰的一面。

340
00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:37.640
Like, if you watch people in the airport or in the grocery store, everyone is a brilliant actor.
比如，如果你在机场或杂货店观察路人，每个人都是出色的演员。

341
00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:42.860
Like, everyone is giving, like, a brilliant performance of picking out a melon.
每个人在挑选甜瓜时，都贡献了精彩的表演。

342
00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.900
You know, they're like, it's true.
你知道，他们就是这样，这是真的。

343
00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.020
They're actually doing it and it's fascinating to watch.
他们确实在那样做，观察起来非常迷人。

344
00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:54.960
The woman who ran my drama program was like, I'm never bored because there are people around.
我戏剧项目的负责人曾说，我从不觉得无聊，因为身边总有各种人。

345
00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.920
Like, I can just study human behavior, you know?
我可以研究人类的行为，你懂吗？

346
00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:58.340
Yeah.
没错。

347
00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.200
That's my favorite thing at an airport.
那是我在机场最喜欢做的事。

348
00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.600
I take a journal and I will just write down what people are doing.
我会带上日记本，把人们的行为记录下来。

349
00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:04.020
Yeah.
是啊。

350
00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:04.780
This is true.
这是真的。

351
00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:05.740
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

352
00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:11.220
Well, I also think we're fighting the distracting rectangle that is taking us away from that.
嗯，我也觉得我们正在对抗那个让我们分心的长方形屏幕，它把我们从现实中拉开了。

353
00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.220
Yeah.
没错。

354
00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.460
Yeah, for sure.
确实如此。

355
00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.300
By the way, Angela, that looks very suspicious.
顺便说一下，安吉拉，那看起来非常可疑。

356
00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:19.320
I just want to, I want you to be prepared that you may get arrested at an airport at some point.
我只是想让你做好心理准备，你可能在某个时候会在机场被捕。

357
00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:22.000
If you're just taking, if you just have a pad out and you're taking notes.
如果你只是拿出一个记事本在做记录的话。

358
00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:23.660
Just be careful.
一定要小心。

359
00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:24.180
That's all I'm saying.
我只想说这些。

360
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.420
Everyone that listens to Office Ladies knows that I keep a journal.
所有收听《办公室女士》的人都知道我一直有写日记的习惯。

361
00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:30.340
I have read it on our podcaSt.
我在我们的播客里读过它。

362
00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:35.920
So, I hope that when I am, like, observing people at the airport and jotting things down,
所以，我希望当我像这样在机场观察人们并随手记录时，

363
00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.460
some Office Ladies member will come to my, will come to my aid.
会有《办公室女士》的听众来帮我，来为我解围。

364
00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.640
If someone's like, write her up.
如果有人说，把她记下来。

365
00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.500
She's up to shenanigans.
她在搞什么鬼名堂。

366
00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:44.000
She's not on her phone.
她没在玩手机。

367
00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:44.940
Yeah.
是啊。

368
00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.200
Why is she not on her phone?
她为什么没在玩手机？

369
00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.580
That's really funny.
那真的太搞笑了。

370
00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.760
I just read this book called Tell Me Everything that I just absolutely loved.
我刚读了一本叫《告诉我一切》的书，我简直爱死它了。

371
00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:56.160
And the theme of this book is that every person's life has a story worth telling.
这本书的主题是每个人的生活都有值得讲述的故事。

372
00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:04.320
And so, it's a collection of small snippets of a whole bunch of different people's lives from this town in Maine.
所以，它收集了缅因州一个小镇上许多不同人的生活片段。

373
00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:08.460
And I just, like, couldn't get enough of it because it was, like, people watching in book form.
我简直爱不释手，因为它就像是书本形式的“观察路人”。

374
00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:09.900
But it gave me an idea.
但这给了我一个想法。

375
00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.000
I'm going to run it by you guys.
我想跟你们商量一下。

376
00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.340
I think I can't do it.
我觉得我做不到。

377
00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.260
Sort of, Craig, based on what you just told Angela.
克雷格，这多少是基于你刚才对安吉拉说的话。

378
00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.440
I had this idea.
我有了个主意。

379
00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.180
This is so insane, though.
但这太疯狂了。

380
00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:19.980
This is so insane.
这简直太疯狂了。

381
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:20.860
I'm going to sound so crazy.
我听起来肯定像个疯子。

382
00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:26.180
I was like, could I, like, leave, I'd have to do this in a city.
我在想，我能不能，我得在城市里做这件事。

383
00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.320
You can't do this in a driving situation.
你不能在开车的时候做这个。

384
00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:33.520
But, like, could I secretly follow a person all day?
但是，我能不能偷偷跟踪一个人一整天？

385
00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:33.600
No.
不行。

386
00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:33.960
Stop.
打住。

387
00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.500
We're going to stop you right there.
我们得立刻制止你。

388
00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.400
And just observe all of what they do.
然后观察他们所做的一切。

389
00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.580
Like, what did they buy at the store?
比如，他们在商店买了什么？

390
00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.460
Like, maybe I start, you know, like, what are they?
比如，也许我开始，你知道，他们是什么样的人？

391
00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.300
Oh, I wonder what they're going to cook.
哦，我想知道他们要做什么菜。

392
00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.520
Television and films, Jenna Fisher.
电视和电影，珍娜·费舍尔。

393
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:48.400
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

394
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.460
And it was all, the plan was all captured on the podcaSt.
而且这一切，整个计划都被记录在播客里了。

395
00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.200
She confessed before she even did it.
她在行动之前就已经自首了。

396
00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:56.680
I can't.
我做不到。

397
00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:03.160
It just, it just, I am similarly, like we're talking about, I am fascinated by the details
只是，我同样，就像我们刚才说的，我对人们的细节非常着迷。

398
00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:03.780
of people.
关于人们的细节。

399
00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.440
Well, I mean, that's one of the great things about The Office.
嗯，我的意思是，这就是《办公室》最棒的地方之一。

400
00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.340
Like Josh was saying, you feel like you're sneaking in.
就像乔什说的，你感觉自己像是偷偷溜进去了一样。

401
00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:09.580
Josh, I was so struck.
乔什，我深受触动。

402
00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:14.280
I said many similarities between our two shows and that I love and I could say more.
我说过我们的两部剧有很多相似之处，我非常喜欢，我还能说出更多。

403
00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.800
The fact that this ends on kind of like a couple of cliffhangers.
这部剧最后留下了几个悬念，这一点很有意思。

404
00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:21.100
Angela, the you and Dwight scene at the end, we have to talk about that scene.
安吉拉，最后你和德怀特的那个场景，我们必须聊聊。

405
00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:22.300
That was magnificent.
那场戏太精彩了。

406
00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:23.520
We got to get there at some point.
我们迟早得聊到那儿。

407
00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.400
Oh, it's so weird.
噢，那感觉太奇妙了。

408
00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:30.020
And one thing that's very, very different about our two shows is we used music to be
我们两部剧有一个非常、非常大的不同点，那就是我们利用音乐来

409
00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:33.580
very emotionally manipulative to the audience.
对观众进行情感上的操纵。

410
00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.600
We were, we were, we're music nerds.
我们是，我们是，我们是音乐迷。

411
00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.480
Like I said, Carter and I, like we are, our connection was musical before it was writing
就像我说的，卡特和我，我们的联系在写剧本之前

412
00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.200
words on a page.
就是通过音乐建立起来的。

413
00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:44.460
Josh, it would, Josh is a complete music nerd and would come and pitch us songs that we
乔什，乔什是个彻头彻尾的音乐迷，他会来向我们推荐歌曲，然后我们

414
00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:44.960
put on the show.
把它们用在剧里。

415
00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:49.240
So I was really struck watching it again, watching The Office for the first time in a few years.
所以重温这部剧时，我真的深受触动，这是我几年来第一次看《办公室》。

416
00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:54.840
The quietness, this, the, the fact that there's no music, the fact that the soundtrack is the
那种安静，那种，那种没有背景音乐的事实，那种原声带就是

417
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:58.860
sounds of an office, it's breathing, it's papers moving, it's keyboards clacking.
办公室里的声音，呼吸声、纸张移动声、键盘敲击声。

418
00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:04.580
There's something so hypnotic, wonderfully hypnotic that really draws you in.
有一种非常催眠、美妙得令人着迷的感觉，真的把你深深吸引住了。

419
00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.660
And you really, it really is voyeuristic.
而且你真的，这真的有一种偷窥感。

420
00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:12.360
You really are there just spying on people and it just works so profoundly well to make
你就像是在那里窥探人们的生活，这种方式非常奏效，让你

421
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.900
you, you're in those characters' shoes and you're not being told how to feel.
让你设身处地地站在那些角色的立场上，而不是被告知该有什么样的感受。

422
00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.180
You're just there.
你就只是在那里看着。

423
00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:22.540
I heard about this thing that's taking off in Scandinavia and it's called slow TV.
我听说斯堪的纳维亚半岛正在流行一种东西，叫“慢电视”。

424
00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:23.620
Have you guys heard about this?
你们听说过吗？

425
00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:30.080
It's, it's basically like long uninterrupted scenes, scenes where people are in nature.
它基本上就是那种长镜头、不间断的场景，人们置身于大自然中。

426
00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:34.760
There's a story being told, but it's like scenes in nature that are just allowed to, I think
虽然也在讲故事，但就像是那些任其自然发展的场景，我想

427
00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:39.840
like as things get so fast paced, people are longing for just like, slow it down.
随着节奏变得越来越快，人们渴望的就是，慢下来。

428
00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:42.100
Like slow me down, slow this story down.
就像是让我慢下来，让这个故事慢下来。

429
00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:44.160
Give me a moment to breathe.
给我一点喘息的时间。

430
00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:50.480
And I, I sometimes feel that after being on my phone too much, just like, oh my God, take
有时候在手机上待太久之后，我也会有这种感觉，天哪，把

431
00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:55.000
this thing away from me and let me just, I don't know, tell me like a longer story or
这东西从我身边拿走，让我，我不知道，给我讲个长一点的故事

432
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:55.380
something.
之类的。

433
00:19:55.680 --> 00:20:00.060
Can I say one thing, just going back to what Jenna's criminal plot to follow.
我能说一件事吗，回到刚才珍娜那个跟踪人的犯罪计划上。

434
00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.100
So this person.
就是这个人。

435
00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.600
To follow somebody for a day?
跟踪某人一天？

436
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:02.900
Yeah.
对。

437
00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:03.460
Please.
请讲。

438
